 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the distribution\nof fines from speed violation monitoring systems in work zones",
    "basePrintNo": "S5892",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5892-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1803, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5892\n\nSPONSOR: KENNEDY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the distrib-\nution of fines from speed violation monitoring systems in work zones\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill will clarify the distribution of fines imposed upon owners of\nmotor vehicles held liable for photo-enforced work zone speeding\nviolations.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSections one and two of the bill amend subdivisions 11 and 12 of section\n1803 of the Vehicle and Traffic Law to exempt the percentage of fines\npaid through the Department of Transportation (DOT) and the Thruway\nAuthority work zone speed camera demonstration programs from a provision\nof law capping the aggregate amount of speeding fines certain types of\nmunicipalities can collect annually, to clarify the distribution of work\nzone speed camera fines to counties with traffic and parking violations\nagencies, and to clarify that the remittance of work zone speed camera\nfines by local governments to the State Comptroller are subject to the\nComptroller's alternative procedures as authorized by the State Finance\nLaw.\n\nSection two of the bill provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe provisions of this bill are necessary to ensure the process for the\ncollection and remittance of fines and penalties collected from the DOT\nand Thruway Authority work zone speed camera demonstration programs\nresult in the intended distribution of these fines and penalties.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nUndetermined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that the\namendments to subdivisions 11 and 12 of section 1803 made by section one\nof this act shall not affect the expiration and repeal of such subdivi-\nsions and shall be deemed repealed therewith.\n",
